---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { company } from '../../data/company';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy statement — Privacy Shield Group"
  description="How Privacy Shield Group B.V. handles the personal data of visitors to privacyshieldgroup.com."
  path="/privacy-statement/"
>
  <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
  <h1>Privacy statement</h1>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <p>
    {company.legalName} certifies hotels on how they handle the privacy of their guests.
    It would be odd to ask that of others and be vague about it ourselves, so this page
    states plainly what this website does and does not do with your data.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. privacyshieldgroup.com is an information site. It carries no contact form,
    no accounts and no login. We set no tracking cookies and run no analytics or
    advertising scripts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Fonts and images are served from our own server. No request from this page goes to
    Google, to a font service or to any other third party, so no third party learns that
    you visited us.
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> or call
    <a href={`tel:${company.phoneHref}`}>{company.phoneDisplay}</a> and we process the
    details you supply, for one purpose: answering you. We keep that correspondence for
    as long as handling your question requires and for as long as statutory retention
    obligations demand, and no longer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mail sent to our address is routed through Cloudflare Email Routing, which forwards
    it to the mailbox we actually read. Your message passes through Cloudflare's
    infrastructure on the way.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and logs</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes technical request data
    such as your IP address to deliver the page and to defend against attacks. That is a
    normal part of serving a website and is covered by Cloudflare's own data processing
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Certification work</h2>
  <p>
    This statement covers the website only. Personal data processed during an audit,
    inspection or training assignment is governed by the agreement with the client
    concerned, including the processing agreement that forms part of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask to see the data we hold about you, to have it corrected or to have it
    erased. Write to <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>. You may also
    lodge a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority, the Autoriteit
    Persoonsgegevens.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {company.legalName}<br />
    {company.street}<br />
    {company.postalCode} {company.city}<br />
    {company.country}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a><br />
    <a href={`tel:${company.phoneHref}`}>{company.phoneDisplay}</a>
    {company.kvk && <Fragment><br />Chamber of Commerce {company.kvk}</Fragment>}
    {company.vat && <Fragment><br />VAT {company.vat}</Fragment>}
  </p>
  <p>
    {company.legalName} is a wholly owned subsidiary of
    <a href={company.parent.url} rel="noopener">{company.parent.name}</a>, registered in
    the Dutch business register under number {company.parent.kvk}.
  </p>

  <p class="meta">Last updated: 9 October 2026.</p>
</LegalLayout>
